From 875b15e6ce96f0f67bda3409a367d0e0eda68616 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KEGustafsson <ke.gustafsson@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:42:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] feat: skip restoring values after a long downtime

A computer without a real-time clock boots with the time it last
saved, so the wall clock can't tell how long the server was off. The
saved file now records the boot id and uptime with the save time.

Within the same boot the downtime comes from uptime and is exact.
After a reboot it comes from the wall clock, and is checked again once
the clock is set by NTP or a GNSS time source: if the server was off
longer than restoreMaxAgeMinutes (default 60) after all, restored
values that live data has not replaced are dropped.
